need other evidence, too.

629
00:11:17,580 --> 00:11:19,660
Letters, books, documents,

630
00:11:19,660 --> 00:11:21,200
and the burials themselves.

631
00:11:21,200 --> 00:11:21,980
The arrangement

632
00:11:21,980 --> 00:11:23,140
of the graves preserves

633
00:11:23,140 --> 00:11:24,020
part of that story

634
00:11:24,020 --> 00:11:24,820
as well.

635
00:11:24,820 --> 00:11:25,320
The money

636
00:11:25,320 --> 00:11:26,300
remained with the dead

637
00:11:26,300 --> 00:11:27,440
woman, and beside

638
00:11:27,440 --> 00:11:28,600
her lay other people

639
00:11:28,600 --> 00:11:29,660
buried in an order

640
00:11:29,660 --> 00:11:30,240
that someone

641
00:11:30,240 --> 00:11:31,700
continued to maintain.

642
00:11:31,700 --> 00:11:32,520
We do not know

643
00:11:32,520 --> 00:11:32,920
the names

644
00:11:32,920 --> 00:11:33,720
of those who dug

645
00:11:33,720 --> 00:11:34,560
the graves and brought

646
00:11:34,560 --> 00:11:35,300
the dead here.

647
00:11:35,300 --> 00:11:36,080
We do not know

648
00:11:36,080 --> 00:11:37,040
what drove them.

649
00:11:37,040 --> 00:11:38,560
Duty, wages,

650
00:11:38,560 --> 00:11:39,640
faith, or care

651
00:11:39,640 --> 00:11:40,600
for their loved ones.

652
00:11:40,600 --> 00:11:41,380
But the city

653
00:11:41,380 --> 00:11:42,660
held together in part

654
00:11:42,660 --> 00:11:43,780
because of their work.

655
00:11:43,780 --> 00:11:44,840
They carried it out

656
00:11:44,840 --> 00:11:45,700
without yet knowing

657
00:11:45,700 --> 00:11:46,540
what was killing

658
00:11:46,540 --> 00:11:47,466
their neighbors.
